## `WorkspaceCargoResolver` — Technical Picture for Spec Design

### 1. `load(path)` — always reads from disk, no caching

`crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs:525-556`. Every call does `fs::read_to_string` + `toml_edit` parse unconditionally; there is no memoization anywhere in `WorkspaceCargoResolver` or its callers.

```rust
pub fn load(root_manifest_path: &Path) -> Result<Self, ManifestError> {
    ...
    let content = fs::read_to_string(root_manifest_path)...
    let doc: toml_edit::DocumentMut = content.parse()...
    Ok(WorkspaceCargoResolver { root_path: rel_path, absolute_path: ..., document: doc })
}
```

Contrast: `manifest_cache` (`crates/callisto-graph/src/manifest_cache.rs:41-55`) is a *separate*, read-only `Arc<dyn Manifest>` cache — `WorkspaceCargoResolver` has no equivalent and is never routed through it.

### 2. `write_version`/`write_dependency` — combined mutate+persist, unlike `Manifest`

`cargo.rs:611-647` and `:649-711`: both mutate `self.document` then call `self.persist(permit)` as their last line, returning one `Result`. `persist` (private, `cargo.rs:713-721`) does `self.document.to_string()` + `crate::atomic::atomic_write`.

This is the **opposite** of the post-refactor `Manifest` trait (`lib.rs:24-39`), which splits mutate (`write_version(&mut self, ...)`) from persist (`persist(&mut self, ...)`) as two separate trait methods — callers must invoke both (see `apply.rs:87-88`, `:121`, and the `ManifestCstEditor` blanket impl at `lib.rs:79-98`).

### 3. Dual-targeting the same physical root `Cargo.toml` — reachable, not structurally prevented

Routing decision is made in `solve_cascade` at `crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs:238-247`, keyed purely on `edge.inherited`:

```rust
target: if edge.inherited {
    DepWriteTarget::CargoWorkspaceDependency { root_manifest: edge.from_manifest.clone() }
} else {
    DepWriteTarget::Manifest(edge.from_manifest.clone())
},
```

`edge.from_manifest`/`inherited` are set per-dependency-entry in `walk.rs:343-372` (root's *own* inherited deps get `from_manifest = inh.declared_in` = the root manifest path; non-inherited deps get `from_manifest = decl.path`, which for the workspace-root package **is the same root `Cargo.toml` path**). So a root crate that both (a) declares one dependency plainly (`serde = "1.0"`) and (b) inherits another (`tokio = { workspace = true }`) produces, in the *same* `plan.rewrites`, a `DepWriteTarget::Manifest("Cargo.toml")` entry and a `DepWriteTarget::CargoWorkspaceDependency{root_manifest:"Cargo.toml"}` entry — different `RewriteKey.name`, same physical file. `apply.rs:108-130` executes both branches in one loop, each doing its own independent `open()`/`WorkspaceCargoResolver::load()` → mutate → persist. No batching exists today (task #8), so each write is an immediate, self-contained read-modify-write — sequential execution avoids clobbering, but only because nothing is cached/deferred across iterations.

The narrower same-*name* collision (a dependency that is inherited being written via the `Manifest` path) is explicitly guarded against inside `CargoToml::update_dependency_spec` at `cargo.rs:303-316`:

```rust
if self.inherited_deps.contains(&(kind, name.to_string())) {
    let root_cargo = self.workspace_root.join("Cargo.toml");
    if self.absolute == root_cargo {
        return Err(ManifestError::InvariantViolation { ... "refusing to delegate to avoid
            overwriting the just-written root manifest with a stale in-memory document" ... });
    }
    let mut ws_res = WorkspaceCargoResolver::load(&root_cargo)?;
    return ws_res.write_dependency(name, new, permit);
}
```
