### 5. No long-lived in-memory doc — each write is single-shot

Every `WorkspaceCargoResolver` in `apply.rs` is constructed, used once, and dropped within a single match arm: `apply.rs:100-102` (version) and `:125-127` (dependency). No instance is held across writes. Within one `apply_version_plan` call the root `Cargo.toml` can still be independently parsed multiple times (once for the up-front inheritance `ctx` at `apply.rs:55-63`, plus once per subsequent workspace-target write) — each is a fresh read, so no cross-instance staleness, just redundant I/O.

### 6. `manifest_cache` is never touched by `apply_version_plan`

`apply_version_plan`'s signature (`apply.rs:45-51`) takes no `Workspace`/cache parameter at all; it calls the free function `callisto_manifests::open` directly (`apply.rs:82`, `:114`). `manifest_cache` (`crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs:75-82`, `manifest_cache.rs:1-28`) is consulted only by `ManifestWalkResolver::build` (`walk.rs:341`) and `Workspace::base_versions` (`lib.rs:158`) — both read-only, pre-apply paths. `lib.rs:80-81` documents this explicitly: *"Never consulted by the manifest-open-for-write path in `apply.rs`, which always needs a fresh, exclusively-owned `&mut` handle."*

