  "expected_pass": "test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed. (persist_call_count_test.rs's one test, cargo_persist_increments_persist_call_count_on_success, passes.)",
  "commit_message": "feat(manifests): add persist_call_count instrumentation, wired into CargoToml::persist

Mirrors the existing open_call_count/reset_open_call_count precedent
(lib.rs:108-124) with its own process-global AtomicUsize, distinct from
OPEN_CALL_COUNT. CargoToml::persist increments it immediately after a
successful atomic_write; an Err does not increment it. The regression
test lives in a new dedicated integration binary (not --lib) since the
counter is process-global and would otherwise race the many unrelated,
non-#[serial] persist() tests already in cargo.rs/npm.rs/python.rs's own
test modules -- the same isolation apply_persist_open_count_test.rs
already documents for OPEN_CALL_COUNT. PackageJson and PyprojectToml are
wired in the next two commits."
}

