DEVIATION FROM AC-015'S LITERAL WORDING, stated explicitly per the calling agent's 'never defer, pick an approach and state it' instruction (mirroring the same pattern T13 already uses for its own AC-016 file-placement deviation): AC-015's literal text asks for the test to run 'under both an absolute and a relative tempdir root,' i.e. to exercise WorkspaceCargoResolver::load's relative-input branch by actually calling load() with a relative path under a real tempdir. This task instead covers that branch's substance by asserting `callisto_model::workspace_relative(...)` directly, because exercising the relative branch via a genuine relative-path load() call would require a process-wide `std::env::set_current_dir` swap that races the ~30 other, non-#[serial] tests sharing cargo.rs's `--lib` test binary (#[serial] only excludes other #[serial] tests, not those). Re-reading cargo.rs's relative-input branch shows it performs no transformation beyond calling workspace_relative(root_manifest_path) -- so asserting that same function directly, on the same input, covers the branch's full behavior with strictly less flakiness than a cwd-swapping call to load() would have. This is a deliberate, documented substitution, not an uncovered gap.",
